ct, anchored on the Eastern Shore, leans Republican by about eight points, and Andy Harris has held the seat since 2011. He faces Democrat Dan Schwartz, a former state treasurer. Harris has raised $2.7 million and holds roughly $1.2 million on hand, while Schwartz raised $1.2 million but ended the period with no cash on hand.\n\nThe only public poll, conducted in July by a Democratic-leaning firm, showed Harris ahead 52 to 39. Prediction markets give Schwartz about a 16 percent chance, and most race raters call the seat solid or likely Republican. The contest drew wider attention in mid-October after a contentious Harris debate moment went viral, giving Democrats an opening, but the district's fundamentals and resources still favor the incumbent heading into the final stretch.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1047, "margin": -9.08}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0918, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0624, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0531, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0408, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0618, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0882, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0539, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.101, "margin": -9.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0704, "margin": -10.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.1137, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.0766, "margin": -10.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.0557, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.0562, "margin": -10.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.05, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.0495, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.046, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.0653, "margin": -10.5}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.0488, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-11", "p_dem": 0.0382, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-12", "p_dem": 0.0538, "mar